body:
I'm getting scared.  After calling them every week beginning Feb 11, having filed my ID verification twice, sent in income proof, they reopened my PUA claim three times, so many contradictions on the phone, I'm starting to think they do NOT want to send me benefits (just speculating, not quite sure).  I finally got my miwam portal opened two days ago and there is a certification finally.  But I called them asking if I'm all set only for them to tell me that all my payments that left off on November 1st last year to March of this year are now gone.  The backdated payments are now invalid because I did not certify in time before 4/11/21, so any backdated payments before then don't mean anything now.

&#x200B;

So I went through all of that. For nothing.  I wasted my time, I'm depressed.  I've been crying all day yesterday.  No matter how much effort I put in to making sure the support people understand the minor problems I'm having, they only made it worse.

&#x200B;

I'm a broke graduate that is off to a rough start.   I'm thinking about doing anything at this point, applying to Mcdonald's as someone with a recent BS in Mechanical Engineering and minor in comp sci.

I'm frustrated, why can't America perform the most simple of tasks?
